solarman-bridge (2.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Settings tab: the inverter's own settings, shown and changed from the
    page. Three groups for deye_sg04lp3: Time of use (power, SOC or voltage
    and charge sources, one value for all six windows), Charge & signals,
    Battery limits. Which settings there are follows the battery mode.
  * API: GET api/settings returns every setting with its description and
    value; PUT api/settings?<name>=<value>&... changes the named ones, with
    the password in an Authorization: Basic header. The request is answered
    when the change is written and the settings are read again.
  * solarman_bridge_passwd sets the password for changes: it asks for one
    (or makes a random one with -g), writes its hash to the config and
    restarts the service.
  * The command that switched the inverter on and off is gone, with
    POST api/command and the power button on the diagram.
  * A model is a list of register blocks with their decoders and of
    settings; the poller sends one batch of requests per tick.

 -- Alexey Volokitin <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0200

solarman-bridge (1.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Inverter commands need a password: control { password_hash } holds its
    crypt(3) hash (openssl passwd -6); five wrong passwords in a row lock
    commands out for a minute. Control does not start without the hash.
  * The power button is the state circle on the Realtime diagram; it asks
    for the password. The control buttons on the Info tab are gone.

 -- Alexey Volokitin <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0300

solarman-bridge (1.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * http { bind } sets the listen address; the template binds 127.0.0.1 so
    the dashboard is reached through a reverse proxy on the host.
  * Inverter commands log the client from X-Forwarded-For when proxied.

 -- Alexey Volokitin <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:50:00 +0300

solarman-bridge (1.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Monitors Deye hybrid inverters through their Solarman
    WiFi loggers: native Solarman V5 / Modbus RTU client on the dispatcher,
    one poller per inverter, live data every second.
  * Several inverters, one config section each; inverter models are one
    file each in src/models/ (deye_sg04lp3 so far).
  * SQLite history: one sample per 5 s kept 30 days, daily energy from the
    inverter's own counters kept for good, per inverter.
  * Dashboard on port 8081: Realtime power flow with per-node tables,
    History charts, Energy pies and daily bars per month (one inverter or
    all), Info. JSON API under api/.
  * Inverter on/off commands, off unless enabled in the config.

 -- Alexey Volokitin <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
